{%- comment -%}
  The "what it is" cell of one subdirectory row. Included by files.liquid
  with `d` = the row; prints one line, never a count (bean `ba9e`).

  Declared (the caller resolved a description) prints bare. Derived from the
  subdirectory itself (`describe-dir.ts`) carries where it came from, so a
  reader can tell the two apart and knows which file to edit; the kinds
  fallback is italic, because it describes the files, not their subject.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign d = include.d -%}
{%- if d.description != "" -%}
{%- if d.kinds -%}_holds {{ d.description }}_{%- elsif d.from != "" -%}{{ d.description }} _(from `{{ d.from }}`)_{%- else -%}{{ d.description }}{%- endif -%}
{%- elsif d.readme != "" -%}described in its own README{%- else -%}_nothing declares what this holds_{%- endif -%}
